@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:backend;error-handling;testing] retry-safe-resource-writes
Production transactions that mutate resource state MUST use `fdb::with_idempotent_transaction`,
covering the whole transaction and its returned result with one receipt. Bodies MUST still tolerate
retries after aborted attempts; mutable resource state MUST be rebuilt inside each attempt.
Expired-session cleanup MAY use ordinary transactions: repeating a committed batch MUST be safe,
and its cleanup counts need not survive an unknown commit result.
Receipt maintenance MUST use ordinary transactions to avoid creating receipts recursively.
Tests MAY use raw transactions to exercise conflicts, rollback, and resource validation directly.

@cc [owner:spolu,notify:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] preserve-fdb-retry-errors
Within retrying transactions, FDB transaction failures MUST reach `Database::run` unchanged through
every resource and API conversion so the runner can decide whether to retry. They MUST NOT be
swallowed, stringified, or converted to domain errors or API statuses before the runner returns.

@cc [owner:spolu,notify:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] transaction-domain-errors
A transaction closure returning a resource or stored-data decoding failure MUST abort its attempt
without committing or retrying. `fdb::with_transaction` MUST preserve the typed error returned by
its closure through the runner. API closures MAY translate non-FDB failures to their API status
before returning them.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:testing;architecture] tests-under-tests
Test implementations MUST live under `server/tests/`, never inline in `server/src/`. Unit tests MAY
be included from source modules with `#[cfg(test)]` and `#[path = ...]` to retain access to private
items.
